# Tokens

The wire format and lifetime rules, shared by every domain that authenticates.
The term itself is defined once in [[/glossary/token|the glossary]].

## Rotation

Tokens rotate every 24 hours, and a rotated token stays valid for a 60-second
overlap so in-flight requests are not cut off. ^rotation-window

## Revocation

Revocation is immediate and is not subject to the overlap above. A revoked
token fails closed at the edge, before any handler runs.

Signature verification uses the current key set only; see
[[retry-policy#Backoff]] for what a caller should do when the key set is
temporarily unreachable.
